@*
    The mark of a captured thing's kind: what an inbox item is before anybody
    has decided what to do with it.

    Ten glyphs on one 16x16 grid, drawn in the library's state-icon voice —
    stroked at 1.6, never filled, currentColor throughout — so they sit beside
    KnowledgeTypeMarker and the state icons as one family rather than a second
    icon set. The one fill is YouTube's play triangle, for the reason
    KnowledgeTypeMarker fills its identity dots: a hollow triangle inside a
    rounded frame reads as a warning sign, and the filled one is the shape every
    reader already knows.

    Monochrome, and that is a rule rather than an omission. It would be easy to
    tint a video red and a document blue; .design/color-scheme.md forbids it —
    a new language MUST map onto the existing tokens and MUST NOT add a colour,
    and badge families get no per-value tone. Shape carries the difference, and
    the word beside the mark carries it for anyone shape does not reach.

    Drawn here rather than fetched, for the reason ProviderMark's header gives:
    a component that needs the network to show itself is no use in a WebView
    with no egress. No sprite, no icon font, no CDN.

    Naming and the tooltip are two parameters, as on KnowledgeTypeMarker.
    `Labelled` is role="img" plus an aria-label and adds no text node;
    `ShowTooltip` is a <title> element and does. A mark beside its own printed
    label — the ordinary case in an inbox row — passes neither and is
    aria-hidden, so a listener hears the word once.

    The shapes inside each arm are written joined, closing `/>` on the line of
    the next, so the svg contains no whitespace text nodes. Same reason as the
    knowledge marker: a mark has no business growing text.

    An unrecognised value renders nothing at all. The set will grow, and a value
    set that grows must never make a row look broken — the caller keeps showing
    the plain word and asks CaptureKinds.IsRecognised when it needs to know.
*@

@if (CaptureKinds.IsRecognised(Value))
{
    <svg class="@ClassValue"
         viewBox="0 0 16 16"
         width="@Size"
         height="@Size"
         fill="none"
         stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="1.6"
         stroke-linecap="round"
         stroke-linejoin="round"
         role="@(Labelled ? "img" : null)"
         aria-label="@(Labelled ? Label : null)"
         aria-hidden="@(Labelled ? null : "true")"
         focusable="false"
         data-testid="@TestId"
         @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">
        @if (Labelled && ShowTooltip)
        {
            <title>@Label</title>
        }
        @if (Slug is "text")
        {
            @* Lines of prose: the note, which is what every source can produce. *@
            <path d="M3 4.2h10"
            /><path d="M3 8h10"
            /><path d="M3 11.8h6.2" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "article")
        {
            @* A page with a headline and columns under it: something to read. *@
            <rect x="2.4" y="2.2" width="11.2" height="11.6" rx="1.6"
            /><path d="M4.8 5.2h6.4"
            /><path d="M4.8 8h2.6"
            /><path d="M4.8 10.6h2.6"
            /><path d="M9.2 8h2"
            /><path d="M9.2 10.6h2" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "link")
        {
            @* Two chain links: a URL and nothing yet known about what is behind it. *@
            <path d="M6.6 9.4 9.4 6.6"
            /><path d="M7.2 4.9l1.3-1.3a2.6 2.6 0 0 1 3.7 3.7L10.9 8.6"
            /><path d="M8.8 11.1l-1.3 1.3a2.6 2.6 0 0 1-3.7-3.7l1.3-1.3" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "youtube")
        {
            @* A rounded frame with the play triangle in it. The one filled shape
               in the set, because a hollow triangle in a frame is a warning sign. *@
            <rect x="1.8" y="3.4" width="12.4" height="9.2" rx="2.6"
            /><path d="M6.7 6.1v3.8L10 8Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "image")
        {
            @* A frame, a sun, and a horizon: the picture every file browser draws. *@
            <rect x="2.2" y="2.6" width="11.6" height="10.8" rx="1.6"
            /><circle cx="5.9" cy="6.3" r="1.2"
            /><path d="M2.6 12.2 6.8 8.6l2.3 2 1.8-1.5 2.7 2.4" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "document")
        {
            @* A sheet with the corner turned: a file, whatever is in it. *@
            <path d="M4 2.2h5.2l3.6 3.6v8H4Z"
            /><path d="M9.2 2.2v3.6h3.6"
            /><path d="M6.2 9h3.6"
            /><path d="M6.2 11.4h3.6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "email")
        {
            @* An envelope: the flap is what makes it one. *@
            <rect x="1.8" y="3.6" width="12.4" height="8.8" rx="1.6"
            /><path d="M2.4 4.6 8 8.8l5.6-4.2" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "code")
        {
            @* Angle brackets with a slash between: source, as every editor marks it. *@
            <path d="M5.4 4.6 2.2 8l3.2 3.4"
            /><path d="M10.6 4.6 13.8 8l-3.2 3.4"
            /><path d="M9.2 3.2 6.8 12.8" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "voice")
        {
            @* The microphone the mobile capture field already draws, so a memo
               reads as the thing that button made. *@
            <rect x="6" y="1.75" width="4" height="7.5" rx="2"
            /><path d="M3.75 7.25v.75a4.25 4.25 0 0 0 8.5 0v-.75"
            /><path d="M8 12.25v2" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "claude-artifact")
        {
            @* A frame with a spark in it: something a session made, not something
               found. The spark is the four-pointed star, drawn as two strokes. *@
            <rect x="2.2" y="2.2" width="11.6" height="11.6" rx="2.2"
            /><path d="M8 4.6v6.8"
            /><path d="M4.6 8h6.8"
            /><path d="M5.6 5.6 10.4 10.4"
            /><path d="M10.4 5.6 5.6 10.4" />
        }
    </svg>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The kind, as a slug from <see cref="CaptureKinds.All"/>. A value
    /// the set has never heard of renders nothing, so a caller may write this
    /// unconditionally beside a word it is still showing.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string? Value { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Names the mark to assistive technology, and only then: a mark
    /// beside its own printed label would otherwise be announced twice. The
    /// caller that has taken the word off the screen is the caller that passes
    /// this.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Labelled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether a named mark also carries a <c>title</c>, the pointer
    /// user's tooltip. Coupled to <see cref="Labelled"/>: a tooltip on a mark
    /// hidden from assistive technology would be a fact only a mouse could
    /// reach.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool ShowTooltip { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>Edge length. A px value by default because the mark leads a
    /// row's meta line at a fixed density, the way the state icons do; a
    /// heading passes an em.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Size { get; set; } = "14px";

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    private string Slug => CaptureKinds.Normalise(Value!);

    /// <summary>The field and its value together, so a listener hears which
    /// fact became a picture.</summary>
    private string Label => "kind: " + CaptureKinds.Label(Slug);

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var extra = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? string.Empty : " " + CssClass;
            return $"capture-kind-marker capture-kind-marker--{Slug}{extra}";
        }
    }
}
